# Task Completed: Chat/Drive Sync Filters

We have successfully added Customer & Project filtering capabilities to both the Chat Sync and Drive Sync pages, making them much easier to navigate as the list grows!

## Changes Made
1. **Header Updates ([index.html](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/index.html)):** 
   - Added [Customer](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/nocodb.js#27-32) and [Project](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/nocodb.js#47-52) dropdown menus to the top of the **Chat Sync** and **Drive Sync** pages.
   - We updated the table headers (`<thead>`) to include dedicated columns for the **Customer** and **Project** information.

2. **Frontend UI Filters ([app.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js)):**
   - Added functions ([loadChatFilters()](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js#47-57), [updateChatProjectFilter()](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js#58-68), [loadDriveFilters()](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js#140-150), [updateDriveProjectFilter()](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js#151-161)) to fetch and inject the Customer/Project dropdown options.
   - Updated the data mapping logic inside [loadSyncConfigs()](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js#69-117) and [loadDriveConfigs()](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/public/app.js#162-210) to locally cross-reference the `Project_Id` attached to the configs with the `allProjects` and `allCustomers` cache.
   - The tables now display the exact names of the Customer and Project.
   - The data array is filtered based on what is selected before rendering the HTML to the table.

## Verification
You can manually test these features on the locally running server:
1. Reload your browser at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).
2. Create some sample Customers and Projects.
3. Edit your Mock Sync Configs to assign them to the projects you created.
4. Go to **Chat Sync**, and verify the Customer/Project columns populate.
5. Use the dropdown filters at the top of the page. The table list should instantly update to match your filters.
